# Hoist ONLY Metro packages to the root: @expo/cli requires them without
# declaring them (Cannot find module 'metro-core'). Everything else stays
# isolated so each app resolves its own React — a fully hoisted layout made
# styled-jsx grab mobile's React 19 during Next prerender (useContext null on
# /404 and /500 in the Vercel build).
public-hoist-pattern[]=*metro*
# Same failure mode for Babel: the React Native preset chain references
# plugins like @babel/plugin-transform-react-jsx by bare string, which
# @babel/core resolves via Node walk-up — fine locally through pnpm's
# hidden hoist, but EAS Build's install lands a layout where that path
# doesn't resolve and the iOS bundle phase dies with "Cannot find module".
# Hoisting @babel/* publicly makes resolution deterministic everywhere.
# Build-time-only packages — no React inside, so no styled-jsx-style
# runtime duplication risk.
public-hoist-pattern[]=@babel/*
